It adapts ideas, and in places paraphrased structure, from the following open-source
projects. No code or prompt text was copied verbatim unless noted.

- HKUDS/DeepTutor (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/HKUDS/DeepTutor
  Engine-decided mastery gate, quiz-ends-the-turn protocol, defer/repair escape hatches,
  intake protocol, typed knowledge points (memory/procedure/concept/design), the
  retention-scheduler protocol, the rule that same-session practice is not a durable
  retrieval, and treating resource text as evidence rather than instructions.
- mattpocock/skills, "teach" skill (MIT, Copyright 2026 Matt Pocock),
  https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
  File-based learner workspace (MISSION / RESOURCES / learning records / lessons / reference /
  NOTES) and its format conventions; "never trust parametric knowledge"; quiz-option hygiene.
- GeminiLight/gen-mentor, GenMentor (CC0-1.0), https://github.com/GeminiLight/gen-mentor
  Goal -> skill gap -> learner profile -> learning-path decomposition.
- stanford-oval/storm (MIT), https://github.com/stanford-oval/storm
  Persona-driven research: perspectives -> grounded questions -> outline.
- THU-MAIC/OpenMAIC (MIT), https://github.com/THU-MAIC/OpenMAIC
  Language-inference rules for teaching language and terminology.
- dair-ai/dair-academy-plugins lesson-generator skill (MIT), via sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills
  Self-contained HTML lesson approach and smoke-test checklist.
- CAHLR/OATutor (MIT code), https://github.com/CAHLR/OATutor
  Bayesian Knowledge Tracing update (re-implemented).
- Math Academy / Justin Skycak's public writing on hierarchical spaced repetition
  ("Fractional Implicit Repetition"): the idea of implicit review credit. Our own implementation and parameters.

Ideas only (no text or code used): Mr. Ranedeer AI Tutor (unlicensed), plastic-labs/tutor-gpt
(GPL-3.0), Anthropic's learning-output-style plugin (all rights reserved).

Runtime dependencies keep their own licenses: fsrs (MIT), networkx (BSD-3), PyYAML (MIT),
mcp (MIT), markdown-it-py and mdit-py-plugins (MIT), Jinja2 (BSD-3), SymPy (BSD-3),
genanki (MIT). Lesson pages load KaTeX (MIT), Mermaid (MIT), D3 (ISC), Observable Plot (ISC)
and JSXGraph (LGPL-3.0/MIT) from a CDN; they are not redistributed here.
